        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>What is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac {2x + 4} {2}]</span> reduced to lowest terms?</p>",
            "readable_text": "What is [MATH: \\dfrac {2x + 4} {2}] reduced to lowest terms?",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (2x + 4)/(2)|= (2(x + 2))/(2); = (2(x + 2))/(2 \u22c5 1); = (x + 2)/(1); = x + 2]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n[MATH: (2x + 4)/(2)|= (2(x + 2))/(2); = (2(x + 2))/(2 \u22c5 1); = (x + 2)/(1); = x + 2]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nWhat is [MATH: \\dfrac {2x + 4} {2}] reduced to lowest terms?\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n[MATH: (2x + 4)/(2)|= (2(x + 2))/(2); = (2(x + 2))/(2 \u22c5 1); = (x + 2)/(1); = x + 2]"
      },
